The --from-dfir patch to dbo-opt. LOCAL ONLY — this is NOT upstream, and the
pod's stock dbo-opt does not have it ("Did you mean '--from-ktir'?").

WHAT IT IS. Stock dbo-opt has two ways in: --from-ktir, which prepends the
dataflow scheduler to produce DataflowIR; and the SDSC-bundle path. There is no
way in for a producer that emits DataflowIR *directly*, which is what scratchy
does. -kEmitSpyreCode on bare DataflowIR fails in mem_track.cpp on
eps.size() >= 1, because nothing has grown the trackers to the run's program
count or seeded the state the SDSC would have provided.

So the flag adds no stage and changes no existing one. It reuses the KTIR
pathway from the point the scheduler would have left off: the outer branch
becomes (from_ktir || from_dfir) and the scheduler half is nested under an inner
(from_ktir). Everything from dbo-grow-trackers down -- GrowTrackers,
ExtractInputSymbols, AdaptSchedulerDfir, WrapProgramDfir -- is shared and
untouched.

Base: ~/tmp/dt (pristine, no from_dfir anywhere).
Patched tree: ~/tmp/dt_src. Three files, +50/-22.
Apply with: patch -p1 < dt-from-dfir.patch   (from the deeptools source root)

THE STANDING DEBT: needing this at all means our DataflowIR enters the compiler
somewhere the shipped compiler does not accept input. The fix is on our side --
emit at a point the stock tool already takes -- not on the compiler's. Kept only
because the user said so explicitly, and disclosed with every result produced
using it.

--- a/dbo/src/Pipeline/Pipeline.h	2026-08-13 21:48:30
+++ b/dbo/src/Pipeline/Pipeline.h	2026-09-04 14:05:42
@@ -169,6 +169,18 @@
   /// Prepend the dataflow scheduler, so the input is KTIR rather than
   /// DataflowIR.
   bool from_ktir = false;
+  /// The input is already DataflowIR: run the KTIR path from the point the
+  /// scheduler would have left off, with no scheduler and no device
+  /// declaration.
+  ///
+  /// There is otherwise no way in for a producer that emits DataflowIR
+  /// directly. -kEmitSpyreCode on bare DataflowIR fails in mem_track.cpp with
+  /// eps.size() >= 1, because nothing has grown the trackers to the run's
+  /// program count or seeded the state the SDSC would have provided. Both are
+  /// done by the passes below this branch, and what the SDSC would supply is
+  /// seeded by dbo-adapt-scheduler-dfir, which reads the DataflowIR itself --
+  /// so this pathway is the second half of the KTIR one, entered directly.
+  bool from_dfir = false;
   /// Device description the scheduler's ensure-device-declaration pass reads.
   /// Optional: empty takes defaultDeviceFile().
   std::string device_file;
